/**
@mainpage PolyGraph Developer Documentation

@tableofcontents

PolyGraph is a C++23 graph execution engine that presents one logical graph across
multiple physical stores. It contains a distributed breadth-first-search
executor, Neo4j and ArangoDB adapters, optional CUDA/cuGraph acceleration,
HTTP and gRPC frontends, and a policy-driven insertion subsystem.

@section documentation_map Documentation map

- @ref architecture explains component boundaries and execution flow.
- @ref insertion_architecture explains insertion queries, routing policies,
  UUID ownership encoding, batching, and extension points.
- @ref build_guide lists dependencies, CMake options, and presets.
- `docs/CONFIGURATION.md` documents runtime JSON inputs and examples.
- @ref testing_guide explains GoogleTest organization and common commands.
- @ref static_analysis explains clang-format and clang-tidy build gates.
- @ref troubleshooting lists common configuration and dependency failures.

The generated namespace, class, file, and call-reference pages cover both the
public API under `include/` and the compiled implementation under `src/`.
*/
